# 50-git.mdc — Git Workflow & Mandatory Update Protocol

---

## 1. PRE-TASK WORKFLOW

Before starting work:
1. Inspect branch status: `git status`, `git branch`
2. Never work directly on `main`. Use focused feature branches (`feat/...`, `fix/...`, `docs/...`).

---

## 2. MANDATORY REPOSITORY UPDATE PROTOCOL

Whenever an agent makes changes, it must evaluate and update the affected documentation files:

| If this changed | Update |
|---|---|
| Task completed or added | `.ai/TASKS.md` |
| Current implementation status | `.ai/PROJECT_STATE.md` |
| Architectural decision made | `.ai/DECISIONS.md` |
| System architecture | `docs/architecture.md` |
| Data structure / payload | `schemas/*` + `docs/data-contract.md` |
| API endpoint / resource | `docs/api-contract.md` |
| Environment variable | `.env.example` |
| Dependencies / setup | `requirements.txt` / `package.json` + `README.md` |

---

## 3. PRE-COMMIT CHECKLIST

Before committing code:
- [ ] Review diff (`git diff`)
- [ ] Run test suite (`$env:PYTHONPATH="backend"; python -m unittest backend/tests/test_pipeline.py`)
- [ ] Ensure no API keys or `.env` files are staged
- [ ] Use Conventional Commit messages (`feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `chore:`)
